Expedited professional licensure for 25LSO-0532, 1.0
military members.
FISCAL NOTE
FY 2026 FY 2027 FY 2028
NON-ADMINISTRATIVE IMPACT
Anticipated Expenditure increase and (decrease)
SPECIAL REVENUE FUND (0800 Fund Shift Fiscal) $50,000 $0 $0
SPECIAL REVENUE FUND (0900 Contractual Services) ($50,000) $0 $0
Source of expenditure increase(decrease):
This legislation requires the implementation of online applications for licensure
for military service members and military spouses. A&I Professional Licensing
Boards is working with a vendor to provide online services for all supported
boards. Because temporary licenses for military service members or military
spouses are not within the scope of work, this would be considered an enhancement
to add this type of application for all twenty (20) boards.
The Professional Licensing Board initially pays for the software from its budget
and will be reimbursed by the boards.
Assumptions:
Costs are associated with online software enhancements split evenly between the
individual boards at a cost of $2,500 per unit.
No significant fiscal or personnel impact to the Board of Pharmacy, the Board of
Nursing, or the Board of Medicine.
